<title>UK: W.H.Smith details Niceday final sale terms.</title>
<headline>W.H.Smith details Niceday final sale terms.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer W.H. Smith Group Plc said on Wednesday that after finalising all details of the sale of its office supplier Niceday to Guilbert, the company would receive 19.5 million stg plus interest by way of a further payment that had been dependent on asset valuations.</p>
<p>In a statement Smith said &quot;the final agreement provides for 10.5 million stg of the monies held in escrow to be released to Guilbert, the balance of 19.5 million stg plus accrued interest to be released to W H Smith.&quot;</p>
<p>A payment of 112 million stg, the bulk of the purchase consideration, was made when the sale was agreed last April.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
